## 🎯  Quick checklist

| ✅ | Item |
|---|------|
| **PMTiles file** is reachable (same-origin or CORS-enabled). |
| **`pmtiles` library** is imported and `registerProtocol()` is called *before* the map loads. |
| **Source URL** uses the `pmtiles://` scheme with `{z}/{x}/{y}.pbf` placeholders. |
| **`source-layer`** matches a layer name inside the PMTiles vector tiles. |
| **Bundler?** → call `setWorkerUrl()` once (shown above). |
| **CDN?** → use `<script type="module">` and the ESM build; no `setWorkerUrl()` needed. |

That’s all you need to get a line layer rendered from a PMTiles vector-tile source in a MapLibre GL JS v6 map. Happy mapping!
